TI  - Erythema Multiforme in an HIV+ Patient on Highly Active Antiretroviral Therapy After Starting Paxlovid (Nirmatrelvir-Ritonivir).
PY  - 2024
AU  - Cáceres AD
AU  - Bono K
AU  - Kothari N
AB  - In this report, we present a case of a woman currently on HIV antiretroviral therapy who presented with oral mucosal and cutaneous skin lesions with a target-like appearance following completion of a five-day course of Paxlovid™ for symptomatic COVID-19 infection. The patient was treated with intravenous steroids and oral antihistamines with mild improvement. However, she returned in one week with worsening skin lesions. The biopsy and infectious workup were non-contributory. It was determined that the patient had developed erythema multiforme (EM), secondary to Paxlovid™.
