TI  - [Sotrovimab in controlling SARS-CoV-2 infection].
PY  - 2022
AU  - Plusa T
AB  - The new monoclonal antibodies - VIR -7831 (sotrovimab) and VIR- 7832 - show an action directly targeting the SARS-CoV-2 spike glycoprotein. Moreover, they strongly neutralize in vitro the wild-type Corona virus variants and the omicron variant. Sotrovimab is a monoclonal antibody capable of neutralizing SARS-CoV-2 as well as other sarbecoviruses (SARS-CoV-1 and SARS-CoV). The administration of 500 mg sotrovimab as a 1-hour intravenous infusion in 291 patients with COVID-19 with mild to moderate severity of symptoms prevented disease progression and the need for hospitalization.
