AB  - The neutralizing monoclonal antibody combination of casirivimab and imdevimab (REGEN-COV) has been reported to reduce viral load, hospitalization, and death among patients with coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19). However, cases of patients undergoing hemodialysis who are treated with REGEN-COV are rare. A 37-year-old Japanese patient undergoing hemodialysis presented with fever and was diagnosed with COVID-19 pneumonia. The patient had end-stage kidney disease due to diabetic nephropathy and was administered a single dose of REGEN-COV. The patientâs symptoms rapidly resolved and was discharged without complications. Our case demonstrates the effectiveness of REGEN-COV as a treatment for patients with mild COVID-19 undergoing hemodialysis.
