AN  - e0c51a7a6c4e38b2b8deaa488aeefb9e010d148a
TI  - Pharmacokinetics of favipiravir in adults with mild COVID-19 in Thailand
PY  - 2022
AU  - Weerawat Manosuthi
AU  - Ing-orn Prasanchaimontri
AU  - Suvimol Niyomnaitham
AU  - Rujipas Sirijatuphat
AU  - Lantharita Charoenpong
AU  - Katherine Copeland
AU  - Tim R. Cressey
AU  - Phongpan Mokmued
AU  - Kulkanya Chokephaibulkit
AB  - We assessed the pharmacokinetics of favipiravir (FPV) in adults with symptomatic SARS-CoV-2 infection without pneumonia in Thailand. FPV dosing was 1800 mg twice-daily on day 1, then 800 mg twice-daily for 14 days. Eight subjects (7 female), median (range) age 39 (19-53) years and BMI 27.9 (18.0-33.6) were included. Inter-subject variability was high but all achieved minimum plasma concentrations (Cmin) above EC50 (9.7 mg/L). FPV was well tolerated; 1 subject stopped prematurely due to rash.
