AU  - Ruiz-Camps I
AU  - Pumarola T
AU  - Abrisqueta P
AU  - Antón A
AB  - OBJECTIVES: To monitor by whole-genome sequencing (WGS) the early emergence of genetic mutations related to a reduced susceptibility to monoclonal antibody-based (mAb) treatment in immunocompromised patients with long viral excretion at a tertiary university hospital in Barcelona, Spain. METHODS: Serial SARS-CoV-2-positive samples (mid-December 2021 to mid-March 2022) from 8 immunosuppressed fully vaccinated patients (for solid organ transplant or hematologic malignancies) with long viral excretion despite undergoing COVID-19 mAb therapy (Sotrovimab®) were selected. WGS was performed following the ARTIC v4.1 protocol on a MiSeq platform. Mutations in the coding sequence for the Spike protein with a frequency ≥5% were studied. RESULTS: A total of 37 samples from the studied cases were analysed. All cases were confirmed Omicron variant BA.1, but one for Delta (AY.100). Thirty-four different mutations were detected in 62.5% of patients within the receptor binding domain of the Spike protein, 8 of which were not lineage-related and located in the Sotrovimab target epitope (P337L, E340D, E340R, E340K, E340V, E340Q, R346T and K356T). Except for P337L, all changes showed a significant increase in frequency or fixation after Sotrovimab administration. Some of them have been associated either with a reduced susceptibility to mAb therapy, such as those at position 340, or with the acquisition of a new glycosylation site (346 and 356 positions). CONCLUSIONS: This study highlights the importance of monitoring for early in vivo selection of mutations associated with reduced susceptibility of mAb therapies, especially in immunocompromised patients undergoing antiviral drugs, whose immune response is not able to control viral replication resulting on a long-term viral shedding, and under a selective evolution pressure. Virological surveillance of genetically resistant viruses to available antiviral therapies is considered a priority for both patients and the community.
UR  - https://www.epistemonikos.org/en/documents/fc96cdba46dbe10cb07070f7eff7ae032d56a39f
